WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.395
The one-line takeaway is that graph neural networks
are not simply fragile,

00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:09.525
they are over-robust: a large part of their
measured robustness is stubborn robustness

00:00:09.605 --> 00:00:13.344
that persists after the node's true meaning has
already changed,

00:00:13.424 --> 00:00:17.162
which conventional evaluations wrongly credit as
good behaviour.

00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:22.293
Bringing the training graph's label structure into
inference through label propagation

00:00:22.373 --> 00:00:27.423
reduces this over-robustness while improving
accuracy and real adversarial robustness.

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:29.691
And with a semantics-aware definition,

00:00:29.771 --> 00:00:34.344
classifying a newly added node carries no
robustness-accuracy tradeoff at all,

00:00:34.424 --> 00:00:38.580
changing how robustness in graph machine learning
ought to be measured.
